---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Documentation · Agent Hooks Protocol"
  description="Start building with the Agent Hooks Protocol Working Draft, schemas, fixtures, and conformance tooling."
>
  <section class="section docs-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Start with the protocol.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The canonical specification and machine-readable artifacts live in the public protocol
      repository. These links always point to the current Working Draft.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="docs-grid">
      <a class="doc-card" href="https://github.com/agenthooksprotocol/agent-hooks-protocol/blob/main/spec/working-draft.md">
        <span>01 · Core</span>
        <h2>Working Draft specification</h2>
        <p>Read the protocol model, events, effects, transports, registration, and normative requirements.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="doc-card" href="https://github.com/agenthooksprotocol/agent-hooks-protocol/tree/main/schemas">
        <span>02 · Artifacts</span>
        <h2>JSON Schemas</h2>
        <p>Validate protocol messages and portable registration against versioned Draft 2020-12 schemas.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="doc-card" href="https://github.com/agenthooksprotocol/agent-hooks-protocol/tree/main/fixtures">
        <span>03 · Examples</span>
        <h2>Golden fixtures</h2>
        <p>Explore representative requests, responses, registrations, and invalid protocol examples.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="doc-card" href="https://github.com/agenthooksprotocol/agent-hooks-protocol/tree/main/conformance">
        <span>04 · Implement</span>
        <h2>Conformance profiles</h2>
        <p>Understand the base protocol, tool interception, lifecycle observation, and test requirements.</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Working Draft:</strong> AHP v0.1 is not a final standard or a stable compatibility
      commitment. SDKs and examples are non-normative; the specification remains authoritative.
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
